    "Source": "\r\n\/*\r\n    Author or source: CSound source code, Stilson\/Smith CCRMA paper.\r\n    \r\n    Digital approximation of Moog VCF. Fairly easy to calculate coefficients,\r\n    fairly easy to process algorithm, good sound.\r\n*\/\r\n\r\nfloat y_1, y_2=0, y_3=0, y_4=0, oldx=0, oldy_1=0, oldy_2=0, oldy_3=0;\r\n\r\nformula_main\r\n{\r\n\tfloat cutoff = exp(2.3 + KNOB_1*7.7);\r\n\tfloat fs = SAMPLE_RATE; \/\/(e.g. 44100Hz)\r\n\tfloat res = KNOB_2; \/\/(minimum - maximum)\r\n\r\n\tfloat f = 2 * cutoff \/ fs; \/\/[0 - 1]\r\n\tfloat k = 3.6*f - 1.6*f*f -1; \/\/(Empirical tunning)\r\n\tfloat p = (k+1)*0.5;\r\n\tfloat scale = exp((1-p)*1.386249);\r\n\tfloat r = res*scale;\r\n\r\n\t\/\/Loop\r\n\t\/\/--Inverted feed back for corner peaking\r\n\tfloat x = input - r*y_4;\r\n\r\n\t\/\/Four cascaded onepole filters (bilinear transform)\r\n\ty_1=x*p + oldx*p - k*y_1;\r\n\ty_2=y_1*p+oldy_1*p - k*y_2;\r\n\ty_3=y_2*p+oldy_2*p - k*y_3;\r\n\ty_4=y_3*p+oldy_3*p - k*y_4;\r\n\r\n\t\/\/Clipper band limited sigmoid\r\n\ty_4 = y_4 - (y_4*y_4*y_4)\/6;\r\n\r\n\toldx = x;\r\n\toldy_1 = y_1;\r\n\toldy_2 = y_2;\r\n\toldy_3 = y_3;\r\n\treturn y_4;\r\n}",
